                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Monster Boy and the Cursed Kingdom[/b] is a perfect example of what happens when developers pour genuine love, creativity, and passion into a game. The hand-drawn visuals are gorgeous, the soundtrack is fantastic (absolutely love the Green Fields track), and the transformations bring so much variety and uniqueness to the gameplay. Every new ability opens up fresh possibilities for exploration, puzzles, and combat.\n\nWhat I love most is the fantastic balance between fun and challenge. The game constantly encourages you to think, experiment, and master its mechanics without making the experience feel unfair or frustrating. There are so many clever ideas, memorable moments, and little details that show just how much care went into making this game.\n\nThis game is pure platforming enjoyment. A phenomenal adventure from beginning to end, and an absolute must-play for fans of Metroidvania type games. I have huge respect to the developers for pouring their heart out into something this special. Highly recommended!",
